WEBVTT

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.020
It is the Puzzle of Fools.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.530
Where am I?

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.160
The door!

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.270
"For those who ascend the tower,
the Gospel Bell shall ring."

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.480
Flames?

00:00:38.060 --> 00:00:40.060
I have to choose a lift, huh?

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.480
A rook?!

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.400
Sure enough, this is a
Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.250
I take this lift up to other floors...

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.490
It's a multi-story maze where
the goal is the top floor!

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.860
For real?!

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:26.890
Rook!

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.670
So that's it.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:36.030
Rook is the bait while I
tackle the Philosopher's Puzzle.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:38.240
Just you wait, Rook.

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:40.490
I'll save you!

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.890
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.640
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.480
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.230
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:13.730
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:18.450
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.660
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.330
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.330
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:27.620
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:29.540
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:32.380
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.880
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:39.170
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:43.850
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:46.100
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.430
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.060
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:56.940
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.610
Brain diver

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:07.410
Brain diver

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:16.000
The Tower of Parting

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.010
Kaito's in trouble!

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:25.760
I planted a bio-sensor on him.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:29.110
Brain activity, pulse rate,
blood pressure, even location...

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.560
All of Kaito's physical
data is transmitted here.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.560
So these values all
show Kaito's in danger?

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:37.510
A solar eclipse.

00:03:37.510 --> 00:03:38.690
Huh?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.330
I, Ana, think the moon

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.740
is trying to swallow up the sun.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.370
If he... that "Rook"
person is the moon...

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:49.810
Exactly right.

00:03:50.990 --> 00:03:53.030
It would be accurate
to say that right now,

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:54.630
Kaito's life is in danger.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:58.060
Huh? He's in danger? From what?!

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:00.840
I'm going to go to him!

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.550
Y-Yeah! Let's all go.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.120
Is that so? Then I shall prepare-

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.220
Convenient, ain't it?

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:13.230
Not knowin' the truth, gettin' used by folks
who ain't what they seem.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.730
It's about time you cough
up the whole story,

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:18.370
Mr. Principal.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.420
Kaito...

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:29.950
All right, then. We've
got plenty of time.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.550
Start from the beginning.

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:33.710
Yeah.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.450
All right.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.640
Sure enough, the lift's numbers
are the floor they go to.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.040
Dammit!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:02.190
Oh, no!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:05.480
At this rate, I'll get
farther away from Rook!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:11.950
Here, too?!

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.310
What is goin' on?

00:05:27.310 --> 00:05:30.010
I can't see the sentiment
of whoever made this.

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:32.150
No... there IS no sentiment!

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.810
There's only hostility
and murderous intent.

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:17.430
Rook!

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.880
Rook! You okay?! Hey, Rook!

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:23.440
Hang in there!

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:25.900
Rook! Rook!

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.720
Rook! You okay?
Who did this to you?

00:06:33.380 --> 00:06:34.970
I'm fine.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:43.740
I guess my mom and dad
were lookin' out for me.

00:06:46.730 --> 00:06:50.510
Thanks to this, I was narrowly saved.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:55.760
What's that?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.780
It looks like this floor
is the only safe one.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.790
Those blades veered off, and
the launch port is sealed.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:08.190
Just what is this puzzle?

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:10.030
The Puzzle of Fools.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:14.420
It's a puzzle made with the intention
of creating Phi-Brains.

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.330
That's what the man who attacked me said.

00:07:16.940 --> 00:07:18.450
Phi-Brains?

00:07:18.450 --> 00:07:22.290
Yes. This place has been
laid with deadly traps

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.020
to spur on the Phi-Brains' development.

00:07:25.570 --> 00:07:27.450
Those who are deceived by the traps

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.590
and become unable to solve the puzzle...

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.000
will lose their lives.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.140
It can't be!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.640
Kaito's been put into a
dreadful puzzle like that!

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.380
The Puzzle of Fools has no prize.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:47.990
Solving the puzzle and making it out alive
is its sole purpose.

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.150
That doesn't makes sense!

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.810
And? What are these
"Phi-Brains" that the

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.510
Puzzle of Fools is tryin' to make?

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.670
Intelligence that personifies the

00:07:57.670 --> 00:07:59.870
golden ratio: the intellect of God.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:03.970
They are the only ones able to
attempt the Puzzle of God.

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.880
The Puzzle of God?
What is that?

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.740
A puzzle inside which
the ancient philosopher

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:12.050
Pythagoras sealed the Book of God.

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:15.040
Pythagoras? You mean Pytha-Pytha?

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:17.560
The Book of God inside the Puzzle of God?

00:08:17.560 --> 00:08:18.560
I don't buy it.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.770
Only Pythagoras himself knows

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.660
what is written in the Book of God.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.400
It's said whoever gets the Book of God

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:30.530
can know the answer to all
the mysteries of the universe.

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:33.370
Controlling the world at will,

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.340
even overcoming death would be possible.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:39.370
Sounds to me like they're
practically God.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:43.870
I, Ana, think that's something
no human should have.

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:47.690
That's probably why
Pythagoras sealed it up.

00:08:47.690 --> 00:08:49.610
But becoming closer to God,

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.630
becoming a God oneself...

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.810
There are those who have
desired that since antiquity,

00:08:54.810 --> 00:08:57.130
and so sought to create the Phi-Brains.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.890
So Kaito is one of those Phi-Brains?

00:09:01.480 --> 00:09:03.730
The principal believes so.

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:08.640
Kaito, Gammon, Cubik and Ana:

00:09:08.640 --> 00:09:11.660
you four hold Phi-Brain potential.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:13.980
You have been called the
"Phi-Brain children."

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:16.550
I, Ana, too?

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:17.750
And me?

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.030
But not me?!

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:22.160
Not me, either.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.110
But right now, Kaito, who has formed a

00:09:25.110 --> 00:09:29.180
pact with the Amulet of Orpheus,
stands foremost.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:31.130
Huh?

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:33.800
So I'm one of those Phi-Brains?

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:35.380
Gimme a break.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.090
There ain't no way.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.260
You think?

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:41.500
That should do it.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.480
Thank you, Rook.

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:45.740
Thanks to that wandering around earlier,

00:09:45.740 --> 00:09:46.940
I've figured out the route.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.940
Hey, do you remember?

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:54.150
The promise we made back then.

00:09:55.390 --> 00:09:57.070
With the wooden cross puzzle.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:01.910
What, that? Of course I remember.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.950
To see you again. And also...

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:07.750
If that guy was around...

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.300
Kaito.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:20.130
Still, there's no way to
even look for him, huh?

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:23.770
That guy's a wanderer, goin'
on journey after journey.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:26.270
Jin Makata.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.160
His name is Jin Makata.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:30.810
Huh?

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:36.300
I know where Jin is now,
and what he's doing.

00:10:36.550 --> 00:10:38.850
F-For real?

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:42.320
You really know where he is?!

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.080
Yeah.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:45.700
Where did you see him?

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:47.620
Is he doing okay?!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.730
Don't worry. He's doing fine.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:54.460
So, Kaito... let's hurry
and get out of here.

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:56.960
You have to solve the Puzzle of Fools.

00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:14.010
All right. You wait here.

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:15.910
I'll come get you once I've solved it.

00:11:15.910 --> 00:11:18.520
Since way back, your specialty
has been making puzzles,

00:11:18.520 --> 00:11:20.950
and mine has been solving them.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.700
Oh, here. These are Nonoha sweets.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:24.830
Eat them if you get hungry.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.330
There ain't no way I'D eat 'em, though.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:30.440
Guess I gotta go up to the 8th floor from here.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.250
See ya.

00:11:36.610 --> 00:11:39.510
Yes. Since way back,

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.010
Kaito has been the Solver

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.510
and I have been the Giver.

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:47.510
That's why Jin cared
for Kaito more than me.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.550
Because they were both Solvers.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:53.240
Now then...

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:55.980
The TRUE puzzle time is about to begin.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:06.490
To me, that summer the three of us spent

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:08.620
together is an irreplaceable treasure.

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:12.270
They look delicious! Like whipped cream.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:17.460
Say, Kaito, show me your
wooden cross puzzle.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:21.130
You mean this?

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:24.710
That's an important puzzle that your

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.750
mom and dad left you, right?

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:27.620
Yup.

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:32.470
I'm making a new wooden
cross puzzle right now.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.450
When it's finished, I'll give it to you.

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.650
Huh? Really?

00:12:36.140 --> 00:12:40.650
And always keep that puzzle on you, okay?

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:43.900
And every time you see it, remember me.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:46.660
Okay! Thank you, Rook!

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:50.170
We'll always be together. It's a promise.

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.180
Yeah!

00:13:07.410 --> 00:13:09.650
Rook didn't come today either, eh?

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:14.220
They said he transferred.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:17.060
I wanted to see him, so I went and

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.490
asked about him at the special annex.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:21.570
And...

00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:24.320
They said Rook transferred!

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:35.580
Kaito... Life is a puzzle.

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.010
It's tough, sad, and
hard, but the happiness

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:43.380
you get from solving its hurdles is limitless.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:46.970
That's how people keep living.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:50.090
I think I'm going to go on another journey.

00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:51.140
Huh?!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:55.040
You can't! I'll be alone again!

00:13:56.420 --> 00:13:58.330
The puzzles will have us meet again.

00:13:58.330 --> 00:14:00.190
One day, for sure.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:04.890
That is your destiny. Your fate.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:10.540
Kaito. Solve the puzzles.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:24.360
Which way next?

00:14:26.250 --> 00:14:28.880
Could it be this route ain't the way?

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:37.480
What?!

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:47.640
So THIS is what that meant?

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.120
Rook!

00:14:58.810 --> 00:15:01.130
Rook! I'm coming to save you!

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:02.640
Don't!

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:06.290
If you do, you won't make it!

00:15:06.610 --> 00:15:07.630
Rook...

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:09.880
Solve the puzzle!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.630
Kaito Daimon!

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.460
Hurry!

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:19.750
I won't let Rook get killed.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.530
We'll make it out alive!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:28.970
We'll live, and the two
of us will see Jin again!

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:45.290
There's no solution for the
route I'm on right now.

00:15:48.350 --> 00:15:49.550
Got it.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.510
Well done, Kaito.

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:31.970
Creating a shortcut of
a route like that...

00:17:17.830 --> 00:17:19.630
Where's the exit?!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:23.810
You really are dashing when
you're solving puzzles.

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:28.850
But you made a grave error.

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:32.100
Though you've
solved the puzzle, the exit won't open.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:35.030
You took a different route
and used up too much time.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:36.170
You...

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:39.440
How did you get here?

00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:44.000
I know this puzzle well.

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:47.250
That's why I called you to it.

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.850
And not just this time:

00:17:49.850 --> 00:17:51.750
to ALL the Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:17:53.660 --> 00:17:56.840
You've overcome your
tests, and have grown.

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:59.610
The project has entered the next stage.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.910
The Armlet of Orpheus will set you free,

00:18:03.910 --> 00:18:05.850
reveal your true self.

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:09.740
The future you, that is: the Phi-Brain,

00:18:09.740 --> 00:18:11.320
Kaito Daimon!

00:18:11.870 --> 00:18:14.990
You were chosen by the Armlet of Orpheus,

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:17.310
and are the true Phi-Brain child.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.830
Kaito, you can become
stronger, more beautiful.

00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:25.330
What are you talking about, Rook?!

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:30.730
But there is something
you fundamentally lack...

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:40.770
The resolve to throw everything away.

00:18:40.770 --> 00:18:43.470
You were supposed to have abandoned me.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.230
What are you...?

00:18:46.470 --> 00:18:48.640
What are you saying, Rook?!

00:18:50.760 --> 00:18:52.530
You still don't get it?

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.530
I am a Giver.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:58.030
A POG Giver.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.780
Rook is with the POG?

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:06.160
I don't believe it! It can't be!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:09.790
Rook Banjo Crossfield.

00:19:10.280 --> 00:19:12.020
Commander of the POG,

00:19:12.020 --> 00:19:14.330
Count Pythagoras's right-hand man...

00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:17.300
He is, in a real sense,
the POG's No. 2 man.

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:21.300
Sure enough, he's a red moon.

00:19:21.550 --> 00:19:24.400
By order of Count Pythagoras,

00:19:24.400 --> 00:19:27.310
he is trying to make Kaito a Phi-Brain...

00:19:28.010 --> 00:19:31.080
to turn the Book of
God over to the count.

00:19:31.080 --> 00:19:32.240
It's a lie...

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:35.320
A lie! A lie! A lie!

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:38.360
You can't believe it?

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:41.070
Or, rather, you don't WANT to believe it?

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:44.580
Kaito Daimon. I command you:

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:48.250
Become a Phi-Brain and
solve the Puzzle of God.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.460
For me.

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:53.080
What... What the hell's going on?!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.940
That you may do so,

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:57.840
you will solve even more
dangerous Puzzles of Fools.

00:19:59.030 --> 00:20:00.220
You cannot refuse.

00:20:00.770 --> 00:20:03.810
Jin is already being held by the POG.

00:20:05.470 --> 00:20:06.920
But don't worry:

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:10.240
If you follow my orders
and clear the stages,

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:13.310
you can throw everything
away and become a Phi-Brain.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.800
If you do that, you can see Jin.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:17.440
Kaito.

00:20:21.630 --> 00:20:22.980
You...

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:40.240
The Kaito who'd die from
a puzzle like this

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:41.880
isn't MY Kaito.

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:45.230
I've saved you this time.

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:46.770
But...

00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:49.110
Never again.

00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:06.680
Kaito!

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:10.800
They look delicious.

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:13.380
Like whipped cream.

00:22:15.340 --> 00:22:18.260
We'll always be together. It's a promise.

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:19.280
Yeah!

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:23.280
Kaito!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:03.830 --> 00:24:06.790
I can't believe he made
Kaito go through this.

00:24:06.790 --> 00:24:10.920
Rook Banjo Crossfield...
I won't forgive him!

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:13.350
I'll strike him down for sure.

00:24:13.940 --> 00:24:18.620
Then I'll show you who's suited
to be your friend, Kaito!

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:21.190
Next time, "The Right of Friendship"

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:25.520
Okay everyone, let's begin
the Party to Cheer up Kaito!

00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:27.170
The Right of Friendship
